i recently posted a video on why i  decided to try the keto diet what i'm  eating what i'm not eating including  some things that are often eaten on the  keto diet and i shared with you how i  avoided that dreaded keto flu all  together but at that time it had only  been three weeks into it so today i am  super excited to share with you my one  month results and also let you know that  in that one month i've also been  intermittent fasting with a 16 8 ratio  every single day so whether or not  you're thinking of starting the keto  diet or you just need some motivation  hopefully this will be helpful for you  but just please keep in mind that i'm  not a medical doctor i'm not giving you  any medical advice i'm only sharing with  you my experience so for today's video  i'm going to be sharing with you the 10  changes that i have noticed ever since i  started the keto diet so i won't just be  talking about the waistline even though  i will address that because a majority  of people who start the keto diet really  do so because of its help with weight  loss but i've saved that part for last  for a very specific reason and that is  that if you want to achieve a certain  image and you're willing to do whatever  to get there you may just end up hurting  your body in the process so if you want  to lose weight get toned and have a hot  body well awesome good for you but don't  make that your motivation make your  health and your well-being your  motivation and your priority you have  this incredible piece of machinery that  no one else on earth has  your body so my hope is that you focus  on loving your body throughout the  process and transforming it from inside  out so with that being said if you like  this video and find it helpful please  give it a thumbs up and help support my  channel and if not by all means thumbs  it down but please give me some feedback  in the comments so that i know what to  work on alright let's get started  number one i am so excited about this is  it completely eliminated my eczema rash  i've had eczema ever since i was a kid  and because i've used steroid creams on  and off my skin has now become kind of  discolored hopefully you can see but  it's like spotted in certain areas  because of that long-term use of  steroids and because i've had it for so  long i've known to avoid the use of  steroids at all costs and so i kind of  just for the most part live with dry  itchy skin most of the time and about  two and a half weeks into the keto diet  i was shocked my skin is smooth it  started to smoothen out to where the  rash the redness was kind of going away  but it was becoming smoother and now  presently it is gone to me that's  amazing because i have had dryness and  just at least some degree of a rash  pretty much every day because i try to  avoid the use of those sorts of creams  and no matter what kind of natural  healing creams and ointments i've tried  nothing has completely eliminated the  rash itself so i am super excited about  this change number two is also really  exciting is my hair has changed my hair  is actually softer it's smoother it  doesn't get as frizzy this is my hair  actually post wash just waking up in the  morning i do not own a curler  straightener any of those sorts of  things and i haven't been using any of  products that are different from what i  had normally been using basically i use  an anti-frizz serum and an argan oil and  that's it i did mention in my previous  video that i had been using collagen but  that's not something that has changed  either because i had been doing that  even before i started the keto diet so  maybe you could say that the collagen  made a difference but for me personally  i think that it's been my diet that has  made the most notable change change  number three just continuing on with the  hair and the skin is that my skin is  smoother i noticed that a few weeks in  that my skin just wasn't feeling as  rough it was just feeling a lot softer  even as i applied like makeup i could  definitely tell that it was smoother i  currently use hyaluronic acid every  single day but again that's not  something that's changed i didn't change  that i've been doing that for several  months so i don't think that it would  have been that from before keto to now i  definitely noticed my skin a lot  smoother and change number four i'm  really excited about this one is that  these skin changes are not just on my  face they're kind of all over my body my  arms are softer my skin just in general  is softer and it improved my keratosis  polaris and if you don't know what this  is it's commonly referred to as chicken  skin where basically you have a lot of  bumps that almost seem like pimples it  can be behind the arms in the backs of  the legs the thighs and it's like  sandpaper like if you touch your skin it  feels like sandpaper and it has greatly  improved this in me i unfortunately i  didn't think this was gonna change so i  didn't take like a before shot to be  able to compare but it's definitely a  bonus that my skin does not feel like  sandpaper change number five is totally  tmi you guys we're gonna talk about  bodily functions so if that grosses you  out skip like 15 or 20 seconds okay and  that is that my bowel movements are  superb i have been having about two  regular bowel movements per day and i've  definitely been packing on the veggies  and the fiber but i think that it can  also be because i have been a lot more  strict about remembering to take my  probiotics on a regular basis because  i'm just going to be honest with you i  had been taking them for months but  really forgetting to take them  90 of the time until i did this  challenge because i really wanted to  focus this month on doing everything  that i could that would kind of heal my  body from the inside out and so i was  very strict about taking them so maybe  it's been a mix of the diet with the  probiotics probably both sorry of  talking about poop makes you  uncomfortable but as a nurse i know that  some people are pretty obsessed about  their poops so just figured i'd let you  know and benefit number six is that i  have way more energy and actually i'm  gonna be honest a few days out it  actually went to an extreme where i kind  of had insomnia this was probably when i  would transitioned into ketosis and it  wasn't like i was anxious or worried  about anything it was just i had way too  much energy and so what i did to kind of  get through this hump is that i started  drinking chamomile every single day  before going to bed and just being more  active during the day to kind of burn  that energy off and that definitely  helped i don't feel like i have reversed  back to being as tired i definitely have  a lot more energy and benefit number  seven very similar to the previous one  is that my sleep has improved greatly i  now find that it's a lot easier to  actually fall asleep but then once i am  asleep i don't wake up as often so again  i think that also kind of helps the  waking up in the morning and having more  energy or maybe it's also that because i  have more energy and more active during  the day and then i sleep better at night  i don't know but this is a good cycle  and i'm loving it as a full-time working  mom sleep is delicious  change number eight is a major one for  me and it has reduced my anxiety like a  lot i remember that when i was in high  school i had heard about hyperthyroidism  and i thought how cool these people can  lose weight easy lucky's and i am so  sorry that i ever thought that because  for anybody that has anxiety and isn't  able to control it doesn't know why it  can be crippling i had experienced  anxiety where i would be in the middle  of the night calm happy and i just have  a sensation of anxiety like my heart was  having palpitations i had to kind of  catch my breath kind of as if somebody  was following you and it wasn't that i  was worried it wasn't that i was  thinking about something that was going  on i was happy i have a beautiful family  and one loving husband it's not that i  was anxious it's that my body  felt anxiety and that's a tough feeling  you guys when you have anxiousness and  you don't know why and you can't control  it you don't know why you can't do  anything about it it kind of made me  feel like i was crazy before i had my  diagnosis i didn't realize why this was  happening to me um i haven't had repeat  labs yet it will happen soon but overall  i feel that change in my body i feel a  lot calmer and to me  this is huge  and finally benefits number nine and ten  we will combine together because they're  all about the belly and it's that i have  no bloating i definitely have lost  centimeters off my waistline but also a  major part of that is bloating because  it's kind of the top part of the abdomen  and before trying the keto diet i had  had bloating on a regular basis this is  my before clip i have a one-year-old and  i gained 45 pounds during pregnancy i  lost most of it but i definitely still  had the mommy pooch  initially my waist measured 75 and a  half centimeters  after keto you can see that my top part  of my abdomen is now flat and this is  because i don't have any bloating and  let's be honest my regular bowel  movements probably helped as well  but as far as the weight loss goes my  waist now measures 67 centimeters if i  did my math right then it's a drop in  eight and a half centimeters in one  month i am really proud of myself for  having done keto plus intermittent  fasting for an entire month but if i've  got to be honest with myself of all of  these 10 changes the biggest difference  that it's made in is  my confidence i would say that that's  the hugest  the hugest the biggest change that it  has made because my first postpartum  journey with our daughter i was so mean  to myself i said things to myself that i  would never have said to someone else  and that led me to do things that i  shouldn't have done too early it led me  to actually injure my body and end up in  the hospital because i was over doing it  and even then i was making myself feel  guilty because i couldn't do it fast  enough and that's where i made that  point that if you're trying to get to a  certain goal but you're willing to do  whatever to get there you just may end  up hurting your body which is what i did  and this time around i've been a lot  more patient with myself i've been a lot  kinder to myself and loving my body  throughout all the changes it's  experienced and definitely for anybody  that's experienced pregnancy there's  some major changes the body is never  quite the same and i'm okay with that  and loving myself throughout that  process and just being proud of myself  and my body for all of these changes is  amazing my hope for you is that if  you're doing this mainly for a weight  loss purposes is that you  really try to focus on healing your body  from the inside out focus on that  nutrition and pack on those nutrients  and really become educated on the keto  diet before you try to change anything  that way you won't injure your body or  you won't do anything that will harm  yourself in the process because the goal  really should be your well-being as a  whole i hope that this video has been  helpful for you hopefully it's been a  motivation and any of these changes may  be experienced by you if you try it out  let me know if you've tried it and what  your experience has been and don't  forget to thumbs up and subscribe for  more videos like these thank you so much  i'll see you in the next one bye

